# fixedbugs, defect 156, lane land186, 2026-10-02 (panel 186 R5).
#
# A record over `BF` naming only `kind` leaves the bit-fields out, and a
# member left out is a member C fills with zero; but no field can name a
# bit-field, so the repair the message gives is not to name it: the record is
# bound `partial`. The note says so, where a plain member's says what C fills.

extern "fixedbugs-156-bit-fields.h"
    record BF  #~ ffi_incomplete_record
        kind: i32

function touch(b: BF) -> i32
    return b.kind

function main()
    print(1)
